    "body": "<!-- PR title: [Type] scope: title, or [Type] [Hardware] scope: title. -->\n\n## Motivation\n\nOn ROCm/HIP (reproduced on AMD Strix Halo/gfx1151), the KV-cache JIT kernel fails to compile because the shared runtime header references CUDA-only shared-memory attributes. The observed compiler errors are:\n\n```text\nuse of undeclared identifier 'cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlockOptin'\nuse of undeclared identifier 'cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlock'\n```\n\nSGLang falls back, so the server may start without the optimized KV-cache JIT path.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Use `hipDeviceAttributeMaxSharedMemoryPerBlock` in the ROCm path.\n- Preserve the existing CUDA attribute path.\n- Keep the fix limited to the shared-memory capability query used by KV-cache JIT kernels.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo model weights or forward math changed. A real `store_cache()` test on gfx1151 copied two K/V rows correctly, and a Qwen3.5 server smoke test with decode graph capture returned `KV_JIT_OK`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThis is a compile/correctness fix, not a performance claim. Tested KV-cache JIT specializations for `num_threads=0, 32, 64` loaded successfully on gfx1151.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThis PR does not change CUDA graph defaults, memory planning, AWQ/MXFP4 kernels, PLE offload, or FlashInfer/AITER. Full CUDA regression and extended ROCm correctness tests remain follow-ups.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format the changed C++ code.\n- [ ] Add unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation.\n- [x] Provide targeted ROCm/gfx1151 validation.\n- [ ] Provide a performance benchmark.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style.\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Get CODEOWNERS and reviewer approvals.\n2. Trigger the required CI tests.\n3. Merge after CI and approvals are complete.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40737067037](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40737067037)<!-- slot:pr-test