  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 8,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/f1fe4621c654b89c62ac27f5061f95bc6b6a136a/python%2Fsglang%2Fkernels%2Fjit%2Finclude%2Fsgl_kernel%2Fruntime.cuh",
      "changes": 8,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/python%2Fsglang%2Fkernels%2Fjit%2Finclude%2Fsgl_kernel%2Fruntime.cuh?ref=f1fe4621c654b89c62ac27f5061f95bc6b6a136a",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "python/sglang/kernels/jit/include/sgl_kernel/runtime.cuh",
      "patch": "@@ -206,7 +206,15 @@ inline auto get_available_dynamic_smem_per_block(T kernel, int num_blocks, int b\n inline auto get_max_smem_per_block(int device_id, bool opt_in = true, bool use_cache = true) -> std::size_t {\n   /// NOTE: we all know this is no larger than 1MB for all GPU, so use uint32_t\n   static DeviceCacheMap<uint32_t, 0> smem_cache[2];\n+#ifdef USE_ROCM\n+  // HIP exposes one shared-memory limit and does not provide CUDA's opt-in\n+  // attribute. Use the HIP limit for both modes while keeping CUDA behavior\n+  // unchanged below.\n+  (void)opt_in;\n+  constexpr auto attr = hipDeviceAttributeMaxSharedMemoryPerBlock;\n+#else\n   const auto attr = opt_in ? cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlockOptin : cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlock;\n+#endif\n   return smem_cache[opt_in].get_cached(device_id, use_cache, [attr](int32_t device_id) {\n     int value = 0;\n     CHECK_CUDA(cudaDeviceGetAttribute(&value, attr, device_id));",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/f1fe4621c654b89c62ac27f5061f95bc6b6a136a/python%2Fsglang%2Fkernels%2Fjit%2Finclude%2Fsgl_kernel%2Fruntime.cuh",
      "sha": "02b95f9e40c4bc9077f6bc8805e1e1487a3eba83",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "@yichiche, could you take a look when you have a chance? Thx.\r\n\r\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-28T17:37:00Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/47110#issuecomment-6476151634",
      "id": 6476151634,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-28T17:37:00Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "weimin023"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "I tried to reproduce this on RDNA4 (gfx1201) and could not. Setup: `rocm/pytorch` ROCm 7.2.3 / torch 2.10, main at `1ab008f5b0`, plus #43679 so sgl-kernel builds on gfx1201. Without this PR:\n\n- `test/registered/kernels/ops/kvcache/test_store_cache.py`: **316 passed**. The JIT `store_cache` module compiles for every row width the test uses.\n\nOn current main, the HIP branch of `include/sgl_kernel/runtime.cuh` already maps both attributes: `cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlock` to `hipDeviceAttributeMaxSharedMemoryPerBlock`, and `cudaDevAttrMaxSharedMemoryPerBlockOptin` to `hipDeviceAttributeSharedMemPerBlockOptin`. That has been there since #41356. So the `undeclared identifier` errors suggest either an older checkout or a build where `USE_ROCM` is not defined for this JIT module.\n\n@weimin023 could you share the commit and the full compiler command line from the failing build on gfx1151? If it does reproduce on current main, the root cause is probably in how `USE_ROCM` reaches that compile, and it would be worth fixing there rather than special-casing this one attribute.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-29T17:31:37Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/47110#issuecomment-6503805738",
      "id": 6503805738,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-29T17:31:37Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "vivienfanghuagood"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Hi @vivienfanghuagood,\r\n\r\nThanks for pointing this out. My previous baseline used a stale local main (7bdd8fe6ec), which was 2,284 commits behind upstream/main.\r\n\r\nI retested the latest upstream/main (0580e941ef) on gfx1151 with ROCm 7.2.4 after clearing the JIT cache:\r\n\r\n    316 passed\r\n\r\nThe test passed without this PR, so the current upstream main already contains the required fix. This PR's change appears redundant, and I will close it.\r\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-29T18:03:17Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/47110#issuecomment-6504502752",
      "id": 6504502752,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-29T18:03:17Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "weimin023"
      }
    }
  ],
